{"parentUuid":"e1ccc51d-4aae-4712-baef-b4a55ec0ec8e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WRPcLjqA3uiyFD51NrFURp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JcsmexQYR5xiZ8FfxDkM1L","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"LLVM BOLT post-link optimization solver performance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8087,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":320,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8087},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":320,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8087,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotmrrFNg1sa98ydUSpH","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a452dda-7514-4902-9495-1aece3b935ef","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:25.273Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4a729d0d-030e-4fe7-bf41-c0c1ef9b6f61","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SL4mUqmkJjVj12yneDEbBr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT LTO PGO march=native compile performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GCC optimization - Gentoo wiki\",\"url\":\"https://wiki.gentoo.org/wiki/GCC_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Interprocedural optimization - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interprocedural_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Small Datum: The impact of PGO, LTO and more for MySQL on a small CPU\",\"url\":\"http://smalldatum.blogspot.com/2024/10/the-impact-of-pgo-lto-and-more-for.html\"},{\"title\":\"Testing 3 Approaches for Optimizing the Performance of C++ Apps: LTO, PGO, and Unity Builds | The CLion Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/clion/2022/05/testing-3-approaches-performance-cpp_apps/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Optimization and New Capabilities of GCC 12 | SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 15 SP4\",\"url\":\"https://documentation.suse.com/sbp/devel-tools/html/SBP-GCC-12/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"LTO - Gentoo wiki\",\"url\":\"https://wiki.gentoo.org/wiki/LTO\"},{\"title\":\"Profile-guided optimization - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Profile-guided_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"From Profiling to Optimization: Unveiling the Profile Guided Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.16649v1\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced C++ Optimization Techniques for High-Performance Applications — Part 2 | by Martin Ayvazyan | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@martin00001313/advanced-c-optimization-techniques-for-high-performance-applications-part-2-6dc2ebf64813\"},{\"title\":\"Usage — Python Performance Benchmark Suite 1.14.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pyperformance.readthedocs.io/usage.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found general information about LTO (Link Time Optimization) and PGO (Profile-Guided Optimization) compilation techniques, but the search did not return specific results about OR-Tools CP-SAT with these optimization flags.\n\nHere's what the search revealed about the optimization techniques you mentioned:\n\n## LTO and PGO Performance Impact\n\nLTO heavily increases compile times, while gcc performance may improve via PGO, although it may as much as double the compile times.\n\nProfile-Guided Optimization can be combined and is complimentary to Link Time Optimization. While LTO expands what the compiler can do, PGO informs it about which parts of the program are the important ones and should be focused on.\n\nLTO provides a performance boost for all the compilers. With small projects, this boost probably wouldn't be noticeable, but for big ones this option definitely makes a difference.\n\n## Benefits of LTO\n\nLTO can give double-digit performance boosts for many programs. Binaries can become much smaller. Startup time may be improved, especially for large C++ applications.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about OR-Tools CP-SAT's compilation performance with the `-march=native` flag combined with LTO and PGO. To find more specific details about OR-Tools CP-SAT performance with these compiler options, you may want to check the Google OR-Tools documentation or GitHub repository directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7afb0a50-6415-47b2-b933-c22cfc92946a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:31.365Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4a729d0d-030e-4fe7-bf41-c0c1ef9b6f61","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8a452dda-7514-4902-9495-1aece3b935ef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JcsmexQYR5xiZ8FfxDkM1L","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LLVM BOLT post-link optimization solver performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"llvm-project/bolt/README.md at main · llvm/llvm-project\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/bolt/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"BOLT optimization technology could bring obvious ...\",\"url\":\"https://developer.arm.com/community/arm-community-blogs/b/servers-and-cloud-computing-blog/posts/bolt-optimization-technology\"},{\"title\":\"BOLT: A Practical Binary Optimizer for Data Centers and Beyond - Meta Research | Meta Research\",\"url\":\"https://research.facebook.com/publications/bolt-a-practical-binary-optimizer-for-data-centers-and-beyond/\"},{\"title\":\"BOLT: A Practical Binary Optimizer for Data Centers and Beyond Maksim Panchenko\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1807.06735\"},{\"title\":\"[1807.06735] BOLT: A Practical Binary Optimizer for Data Centers and Beyond\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.06735\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use BOLT, Binary Optimization and Layout Tool - The New Stack\",\"url\":\"https://thenewstack.io/how-to-use-bolt-binary-optimization-and-layout-tool/\"},{\"title\":\"[llvm-dev] [RFC] Propeller: A frame work for Post Link Optimizations\",\"url\":\"https://lists.llvm.org/pipermail/llvm-dev/2019-September/135393.html\"},{\"title\":\"BOLT: a practical binary optimizer for data centers and beyond | Proceedings of the 2019 IEEE/ACM International Symposium on Code Generation and Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.5555/3314872.3314876\"},{\"title\":\"llvm-project/bolt at main · llvm/llvm-project\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/bolt\"},{\"title\":\"BOLT - Binary Optimizer for Linux Kernel Maksim Panchenko Meta, Inc ⚡\",\"url\":\"https://lpc.events/event/18/contributions/1921/attachments/1465/3154/BOLT%20for%20Linux%20Kernel%20LPC%202024%20Final.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about LLVM BOLT post-link optimization and solver performance:\n\n## Overview\n\nBOLT is a post-link optimizer developed to speed up large applications. It achieves the improvements by optimizing application's code layout based on execution profile gathered by sampling profiler, such as Linux perf tool.\n\n## Performance Results\n\nThe performance improvements from BOLT are substantial. For the GCC and Clang compilers, BOLT speeds up their binaries by up to 20.4% on top of FDO and LTO, and up to 52.1% if the binaries are built without FDO and LTO. For data-center applications specifically, BOLT achieves up to 8.0% performance speedups on top of profile-guided function reordering and LTO.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\nBOLT disassembles functions and reconstructs the control flow graph (CFG) before it runs optimizations. Since this is a nontrivial task, especially when indirect branches are present, it relies on certain heuristics to accomplish it. BOLT runs many internal passes in parallel.\n\n## Complementary Benefits\n\nUtilizing sample-based profiling, BOLT boosts the performance of real-world applications even for highly optimized binaries built with both feedback-driven optimizations (FDO) and link-time optimizations (LTO).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"edc7847b-465a-487e-9bd6-388eef5be869","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:31.798Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a452dda-7514-4902-9495-1aece3b935ef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e1ccc51d-4aae-4712-baef-b4a55ec0ec8e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ET6oUzCyDjhKbeEsi86LVK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PGO profile-guided optimization SAT solver corpus design\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"From Profiling to Optimization: Unveiling the Profile Guided Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.16649v1\"},{\"title\":\"Profile-guided optimization - The Go Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://go.dev/doc/pgo\"},{\"title\":\"[2112.14679] Profile Guided Optimization without Profiles: A Machine Learning Approach\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2112.14679\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started with Profile Guided Optimization – text/plain\",\"url\":\"https://textslashplain.com/2016/01/10/getting-started-with-profile-guided-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"Profile-guided optimization - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Profile-guided_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO)\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/cpp-compiler/developer-guide-reference/2021-8/profile-guided-optimization-pgo.html\"},{\"title\":\"Proposal: profile-guided optimization\",\"url\":\"https://go.googlesource.com/proposal/+/master/design/55022-pgo.md\"},{\"title\":\"kindatechnical() | Optimizing Compiler Design - Profile-Guided Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://kindatechnical.com/optimizing-compiler-design/profile-guided-optimization.html\"},{\"title\":\"Profile-Guided Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.graalvm.org/latest/reference-manual/native-image/optimizations-and-performance/PGO/\"},{\"title\":\"[2507.16649] From Profiling to Optimization: Unveiling the Profile Guided Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16649\"}]\n\nI found search results related to Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO), though the specific combination of all elements in your query (PGO, SAT solver, and corpus design) didn't appear together in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO)\n\nProfile Guided Optimization (PGO) uses runtime profiling to inform compiler decisions, effectively combining static analysis with actual execution behavior to enhance performance. Runtime profiles — acquired through instrumentation or hardware- and software-assisted sampling — provide detailed insights into control flow, branch predictions, and memory access patterns.\n\n## Corpus Design for PGO\n\nRegarding corpus design, for best results, it is important that profiles are representative of actual behavior in the application's production environment. Using an unrepresentative profile is likely to result in a binary with little to no improvement in production. One example involved creating a folder with files that reasonably represent the types of data that would be processed, as a fine corpus of data with which to begin.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about SAT solver optimization with PGO or how corpus design applies to SAT solver development. If you're looking for research on optimizing SAT solvers using profile-guided optimization with test corpus design, you may want to search for academic papers on SAT solver optimization or compiler optimization for constraint solvers specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c58236cb-ab67-408e-a59c-63950407983d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:31.848Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e1ccc51d-4aae-4712-baef-b4a55ec0ec8e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ea245302-4aa4-4816-bdad-58bee12e9344","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0178pKVvE3bFs98UrcBLdciY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools build from source CMake Bazel 9.15 instructions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Compiling Bazel from Source\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/install/compile-source\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/bazel-to-cmake · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/bazel-to-cmake\"},{\"title\":\"Bridging a cmake build to a bazel build\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/bazel-discuss/c/LP9tyCws_cg\"},{\"title\":\"Building a CMake project using Bazel · Issue #16347 · bazelbuild/bazel\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/16347\"},{\"title\":\"Bazel Tutorial: Build a C++ Project\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/start/cpp\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tazzledazzle/cmake_to_bazel\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tazzledazzle/cmake_to_bazel\"},{\"title\":\"Bazel from the Eyes of a Cpp dev - Jennifer Chukwu\",\"url\":\"https://jenniferchukwu.com/posts/bazel\"},{\"title\":\"Choosing a Build System for C++: CMake, Bazel, Meson, and Beyond · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/MangaD/26ef92a1e1efd967c3e0188dc0591e83\"},{\"title\":\"Invoking Bazel Build from Cmake\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/bazel-discuss/c/IQgdfs7kDcY\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - gangliao/bazel.cmake: bazel.cmake mimics the behavior of bazel to simplify the usability of CMake · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gangliao/bazel.cmake\"}]\n\nThe search results provide general information about Bazel and CMake build systems, but don't specifically address OR-Tools version 9.15 build instructions. Let me search more specifically for OR-Tools documentation.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Opzet/OR-Tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Opzet/OR-Tools\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools at main · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/main\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/cmake at main · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/main/cmake\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools at v9.5\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/v9.5\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - reachatul/or_tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/reachatul/or_tools\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools module - github.com/google/or-tools - Go Packages\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools at v9.11 · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/v9.11\"}]\n\nNow let me search for the official OR-Tools installation page to get specific instructions.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/cmake/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/cmake/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/cmake at main · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/main/cmake\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/cmake at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/cmake\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools C++ on Linux | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/cpp/source_linux\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools C++ on Windows | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/cpp/source_windows\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools Python on MacOS | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/python/source_mac\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools C++ on MacOS | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/cpp/source_mac\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools Python on Windows | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/python/source_windows\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools .Net on Linux | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/dotnet/source_linux\"},{\"title\":\"Building from source OR-Tools Java on MacOS | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/java/source_mac\"}]\n\nNow let me search for OR-Tools Bazel build instructions specifically.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/bazel/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/bazel/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - or-tools/bazel_or-tools: Bazel Template with OR-Tools integration\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/or-tools/bazel_or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - bazelbuild/buildtools: A bazel BUILD file formatter and editor · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/bazelbuild/buildtools\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - bazelbuild/bazel: a fast, scalable, multi-language and extensible build system · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel\"},{\"title\":\"Compiling Bazel from Source\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/install/compile-source\"},{\"title\":\"bazel/tools at master · bazelbuild/bazel\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/tree/master/tools\"},{\"title\":\"bazel/tools/BUILD at master · bazelbuild/bazel\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/master/tools/BUILD\"},{\"title\":\"buildtools module - github.com/bazelbuild/buildtools - Go Packages\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/bazelbuild/buildtools\"},{\"title\":\"bazel/tools/build_defs/repo/git.bzl at master · bazelbuild/bazel\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/master/tools/build_defs/repo/git.bzl\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jin/awesome-bazel: A curated list of Bazel rules, tooling and resources. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jin/awesome-bazel\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I've found comprehensive information about OR-Tools build instructions for both CMake and Bazel. Here's a summary of what I found:\n\n## OR-Tools Build Instructions\n\nOR-Tools v9.15 has been released. Here are the build options available:\n\n### CMake Build\n\nOR-Tools currently provides Bazel and CMake support. OR-Tools comes with a CMake-based build (CMakeLists.txt) that can be used on a wide range of platforms. CMake works by generating native Makefiles or build projects that can be used in the compiler environment of your choice. You can either build OR-Tools with CMake as a standalone project or incorporate it into an existing CMake project.\n\nCMake >= 3.24 is required along with a C++20 compiler (GCC 10 or later, MSVC 2022 or later).\n\nOR-Tools depends on several mandatory libraries. You can either compile them all at configure time using the option -DBUILD_DEPS=ON (OFF by default) or compile some of them using specific options.\n\nTo set options and parameters, use -D<Parameter_name>=<value>. All CMake options are passed at configure time by running cmake -S. -B<your_chosen_build_directory> -DOPTION_ONE=ON -DOPTION_TWO=OFF before running cmake --build <your_chosen_build_directory>\n\n### Bazel Build\n\nOR-Tools comes with a Bazel based build (WORKSPACE) that can be used on a wide range of platforms. If you don't have Bazel installed already, you can download it for free from https://bazel.build/.\n\nBazel >= 5.4.0 is required along with a compiler with C++17 support.\n\nCurrently OR-Tools Bazel doesn't support Python, Java nor .Net, please use the Makefile or CMake based build instead.\n\nFor detailed platform-specific instructions, you can refer to the official documentation at https://developers.google.com/optimization/introduction/installing.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ee96a9dd-df76-472d-bc11-31ef659184a7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:38.461Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea245302-4aa4-4816-bdad-58bee12e9344","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
