{"parentUuid":"a0b1f1cd-dd68-4ab3-97f6-f180697202c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DC5ESJ7s5YLwU7oz54gmwj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" issue github performance compile flags self-build benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - nordlow/compiler-benchmark: Benchmarks compilation speeds of different combinations of languages and compilers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nordlow/compiler-benchmark\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/benchmark: A microbenchmark support library · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/benchmark\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - miyuki/gcc-performance: Tools for benchmarking and profiling GCC · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/miyuki/gcc-performance\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ldionne/metabench: A simple framework for compile-time benchmarks · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ldionne/metabench\"},{\"title\":\"Investigate performance impact of compiler flags · Issue #10608 · paritytech/substrate\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/paritytech/substrate/issues/10608\"},{\"title\":\"How to run benchmarks using custom build configuration? · Issue #1029 · dotnet/BenchmarkDotNet\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dotnet/BenchmarkDotNet/issues/1029\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - gradle/performance-comparisons: A set of synthetic projects used to benchmark Gradle against other build tools · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/gradle/performance-comparisons\"},{\"title\":\"Git Performance Issues | Compile N Run\",\"url\":\"https://www.compilenrun.com/docs/devops/git/git-troubleshooting/git-performance-issues/\"},{\"title\":\"CPP/C++ Compiler Flags and Options\",\"url\":\"https://caiorss.github.io/C-Cpp-Notes/compiler-flags-options.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - scala/compiler-benchmark: Benchmarks for scalac · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/scala/compiler-benchmark\"}]\n\nThe search results returned information about various compiler and build benchmarking tools and projects, but do not contain specific results about an \"or-tools\" GitHub issue related to performance compile flags, self-build, and benchmarking.\n\nThe results include:\n- General compiler benchmark frameworks (like metabench for C++, compiler-benchmark for various languages)\n- Google's benchmark library documentation with compiler flag configurations\n- Various performance investigation issues from other projects\n\nHowever, none of these results specifically address an \"or-tools\" issue on GitHub regarding performance, compile flags, self-build, and benchmarking. To find that specific GitHub issue, you might want to try:\n\n1. Searching directly on GitHub's website at https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues\n2. Using a more specific search query that includes \"google/or-tools\" \n3. Searching for specific issue numbers if you have them\n\nWould you like me to perform another web search with a different query to find the or-tools specific issue?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"34f659ca-391f-40b5-83e9-d88a67b24996","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:10.649Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0b1f1cd-dd68-4ab3-97f6-f180697202c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bf123359-6c04-4faa-8e91-98c5a92b3bee","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014wCunn8rF8BcMfXyWjNQtB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CMake INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE LTO march native\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION — CMake 4.3.2 Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/prop_tgt/INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION.html\"},{\"title\":\"Step 6: In-Depth System Introspection — CMake 4.3.2 Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/guide/tutorial/In-Depth%20System%20Introspection.html\"},{\"title\":\"Compile flags in the linking command for link time optimization - Usage - CMake Discourse\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.cmake.org/t/compile-flags-in-the-linking-command-for-link-time-optimization/9413\"},{\"title\":\"Interprocedural optimization - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interprocedural_optimization\"},{\"title\":\"How to Enable Link Time Optimization (LTO) with CMake: Global Setup for All Compilers Without Manual Flags – Fix Missing -lto in Generated Makefiles\",\"url\":\"https://www.w3tutorials.net/blog/how-do-i-enable-link-time-optimization-lto-with-cmake/\"},{\"title\":\"CheckIPOSupported — CMake 4.3.2 Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/module/CheckIPOSupported.html\"},{\"title\":\"A Guide to Interprocedural Optimization Checks in CMake\",\"url\":\"https://runebook.dev/en/docs/cmake/module/checkiposupported\"},{\"title\":\"CMake Interprocedural Optimization (LTO) with static libraries uses the wrong tools · Issue #11143 · emscripten-core/emscripten\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/issues/11143\"},{\"title\":\"Setting compiler flags in CMakeLists.txt - Usage - CMake Discourse\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.cmake.org/t/setting-compiler-flags-in-cmakelists-txt/8820\"},{\"title\":\"INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION — CMake 3.9.6 Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cmake.org/cmake/help/v3.9/prop_tgt/INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's information about CMake interprocedural optimization and related compiler flags:\n\n## INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION\n\nINTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION enables interprocedural optimization for a target if the compiler supports it. CMake provides a unified interface called Interprocedural Optimization (IPO), which is the CMake term for LTO.\n\n## Setting Up IPO/LTO in CMake\n\nUse the CheckIPOSupported module before enabling interprocedural optimization on targets to ensure the compiler supports IPO/LTO. CMake's IPO support improved significantly in version 3.9 (2017), and for reliable LTO, use CMake 3.13 or newer.\n\n## CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE\n\nMany developers hardcode compiler flags like -flto in CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, but this breaks portability: MSVC ignores -flto and requires /GL (compile) and /LTCG (link), while GCC/Clang ignore /GL and need -flto at both compile and link time.\n\n## Important Notes on Compiler Flags\n\nRegarding the `-march=native` flag: CMake may add its own optimization flags (like -O3) in addition to those specified in CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, which can cause unexpected behavior.\n\nCMake does not know about every IPO/LTO flag on every compiler, so better results can often be achieved with individual tuning for a known toolchain.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"24b751b4-d2d7-49ad-bdc2-97d9bf44858e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:11.874Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf123359-6c04-4faa-8e91-98c5a92b3bee","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0cbfb672-c6d6-49b9-a34d-fea5c2fe064a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Z6h1UfNNtw4KxGfkkL2ix","type":"tool_result","content":"# PGO Build Workflow for Clang/LLVM\n\n## Four-Stage Process\n\n**Stage 1: Standard Release Build**\nBuild a baseline Clang without instrumentation using standard Release configuration. Compile the `all` target to ensure all supporting libraries are available.\n\n**Stage 2: Instrumented Build**\nConfigure with these CMake flags:\n- `-DLLVM_BUILD_INSTRUMENTED=IR` (enables instrumentation)\n- `-DLLVM_BUILD_RUNTIME=No` (disables problematic projects)\n- `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/path/to/stage1/clang`\n- `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/path/to/stage1/clang++`\n\nBuild only the `clang` target and supporting tools needed for your benchmark.\n\n**Stage 3: Profile Collection & Merge**\nRun your benchmark workload using the Stage 2 instrumented Clang. The documentation recommends:\n- Executing `check-clang` and `check-llvm` tests\n- Performing a full Clang/LLVM rebuild with the instrumented compiler\n\nCreate a Stage 3 build directory using Stage 2's compilers, then build the `all` target for comprehensive coverage.\n\nMerge generated `*.profraw` files using: `\"/path/to/stage1/llvm-profdata merge -output=/path/to/output/profdata.prof path/to/stage2/profiles/*.profraw\"`\n\n**Stage 4: Final Optimized Build**\nApply these CMake arguments:\n- `-DLLVM_PROFDATA_FILE=/path/to/output/profdata.prof`\n- `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/path/to/stage1/clang`\n- `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/path/to/stage1/clang++`\n\n## Workload Selection Guidance\n\n\"PGO does best when the profiles gathered represent how the user plans to use the compiler.\" Tailor your benchmark to match your actual use case—generic profiles may not optimize for specific target architectures or workflows."}]},"uuid":"00182db6-6f52-4d35-8b7f-efd1ea120b85","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:14.429Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cbfb672-c6d6-49b9-a34d-fea5c2fe064a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8fc21dda-a4d1-4d45-b08d-30da3a619e45","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012dDZp753r3ANV7czBG31Su","type":"tool_result","content":"# C++ Performance Optimization Results Summary\n\n## Test Setup\nThe article tested three optimization techniques on **clangd** (an LLVM-based language server) across multiple compilers on Windows, measuring execution time for typical code analysis tasks.\n\n## Measured Speedups by Technique\n\n### Link-Time Optimization (LTO)\n- **MSVC 2022**: 73.6s → 55.3s (**25% faster**)\n- **MinGW GCC**: 56.7s → 55.0s (**3% faster**)\n- **Clang-cl**: 70.8s → 63.2s (**11% faster**)\n- **Clang (MinGW)**: 50.1s → 49.1s (**2% faster**)\n\n### Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO)\n- **Clang-cl (PGO alone)**: 70.8s → 49.6s (**30% faster**)\n- **Clang (MinGW, PGO alone)**: 50.1s → 46.1s (**8% faster**)\n- **MinGW GCC**: Showed modest gains without additional LTO\n\n### Combined LTO + PGO\n- **Clang-cl**: 70.8s → 46.1s (**35% faster**)\n- **Clang (MinGW)**: 50.1s → 41.4s (**17% faster**)\n\n### Unity Builds\n- Minimal performance gains; clang with PGO+LTO+Unity: 40.3s versus 41.4s without\n- Notable benefit: **build time reduced from 55 to 45 minutes**\n\n## Key Insight\nResults varied significantly by compiler. The authors note that \"the effect of PGO is hard to predict\" and recommend experimenting with multiple combinations rather than assuming consistent results across tools."}]},"uuid":"82d4a250-543e-478e-bc45-0b0676524790","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:21.667Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8fc21dda-a4d1-4d45-b08d-30da3a619e45","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
