{"parentUuid":"b6045edb-5124-42cf-83d6-3f7bb0ad1bb8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ozyutetdqGcikFPqcPWXk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" pyx pyx wheel manylinux2014 build scripts compiled\"\n\nNo links found.\n\nI performed a web search for your query about or-tools, pyx files, wheel distributions, and manylinux2014 builds, but unfortunately the search didn't return any visible results that I can access or display to you.\n\nIf you're looking for information about building or-tools with Cython (.pyx files) and creating manylinux2014-compatible wheel distributions, you might want to try:\n- Checking the official OR-Tools GitHub repository and its build documentation\n- Looking at the build scripts in the OR-Tools source code directly\n- Consulting the OR-Tools documentation on PyPI\n\nWould you like me to search for something more specific, such as \"OR-Tools Python wheel building\" or \"or-tools GitHub build scripts\"?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3138f03a-e444-41cf-9752-d5b012f3ca46","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:40.565Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b6045edb-5124-42cf-83d6-3f7bb0ad1bb8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"34909c19-6b74-49f2-b8ae-0dff10fc1925","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WcFG2kSdCkX6Jkvm18d4Pu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"AVX-VNNI\" \"AVX-512\" SAT solver benefit instruction set\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AVX-512 - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AVX-512\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Vector Extensions - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advanced_Vector_Extensions\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - twest820/AVX-512: AVX-512 documentation beyond what Intel provides · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/twest820/AVX-512\"},{\"title\":\"AVX-512 - Chessprogramming wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.chessprogramming.org/AVX-512\"},{\"title\":\"Solved: What is the different between AVX-VNNI and AVX512-VNNI ? - Intel Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.intel.com/t5/Mobile-and-Desktop-Processors/What-is-the-different-between-AVX-VNNI-and-AVX512-VNNI/td-p/1460968\"},{\"title\":\"AVX512 VNNI: This instruction boosts ML performance by 2X\",\"url\":\"https://iq.opengenus.org/avx512-vnni/\"},{\"title\":\"AVX-512 Vector Neural Network Instructions (VNNI) - x86 - WikiChip\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikichip.org/wiki/x86/avx512_vnni\"},{\"title\":\"Intel's AVX-512 use cases (Part1) - by Albert\",\"url\":\"https://albertvilella.substack.com/p/intels-avx-512-use-cases-part1\"},{\"title\":\"AVX-512\",\"url\":\"https://iq.opengenus.org/avx512/\"},{\"title\":\"[API Proposal]: Add support for AVX-512 VNNI hardware instructions · Issue #86849 · dotnet/runtime\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/86849\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about AVX-VNNI, AVX-512, and their relationship to SAT solvers:\n\n## AVX-VNNI and AVX-512 Overview\n\nAVX-VNNI is not part of the AVX-512 suite, it does not require AVX-512F and can be implemented independently. AVX-VNNI is a VEX-coded variant of the AVX512-VNNI instruction set extension that provides the same sets of operations as their AVX-512 counterparts, but are limited to 256-bit vectors.\n\n## Primary Use Cases\n\nThe search results primarily focus on the neural network acceleration benefits of these instruction sets rather than SAT solver applications. AVX-512 Vector Neural Network Instructions (VNNI) provide vector instructions for deep learning. AVX512 VNNI is designed to accelerate convolutional neural network for INT8 inference.\n\n## Key Benefits for Data-Parallel Operations\n\nAVX-512 and AVX-512VL's primary advantage over previous instruction sets (AVX, AVX2, and FMA) is arguably reduction in register spilling due to expansion from 16 ymm to 32 zmm registers and the addition of eight mask registers.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain specific information about how AVX-VNNI or AVX-512 instructions might benefit SAT solvers specifically. The available documentation focuses on their application in neural networks and deep learning rather than constraint satisfaction problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a5f9ae41-612d-4d8a-ba66-3512d8147869","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:43.616Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"34909c19-6b74-49f2-b8ae-0dff10fc1925","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f6eba9d4-40a4-4142-ae7c-3ea8cee32f8c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017B37JKAjjW6LJJz4dTkZY5","type":"tool_result","content":"# Compile Flags Analysis\n\nBased on my review of the BUILD.bazel file content provided, **I found no explicit compile flags, copts, or linkopts mentioning optimization levels, LTO (Link Time Optimization), march, or release optimization settings**.\n\nThe file contains Bazel build target definitions for the OR-Tools SAT solver library, including:\n- Library declarations (`cc_library`)\n- Test targets (`cc_test`)\n- Protocol buffer definitions (`proto_library`, `cc_proto_library`, etc.)\n- Dependencies specifications\n\nHowever, none of these targets explicitly define optimization-related compiler options in the visible portion of the BUILD.bazel file. Any optimization settings for this project would likely be configured through:\n- Bazel configuration files (`.bazelrc`)\n- Command-line flags passed during build invocation\n- Workspace-level settings in other configuration files not shown in this excerpt"}]},"uuid":"9a5fe5b1-2d84-43cb-972b-f77982ce5181","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:43.965Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f6eba9d4-40a4-4142-ae7c-3ea8cee32f8c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"908c9e42-eb4d-49ca-9334-1bee16279f1a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8cdae05-aaaa-4408-8a9a-59c4a4939d97","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FDGmFLb2LGkmLiHuaWnRS3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google OR-Tools internal build flags release Bazel BUILD optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Commands and Options | Bazel\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/docs/user-manual\"},{\"title\":\"Best practice to specify Bazel compiler and linker flags\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/bazel-discuss/c/2G_8xPAGtTg\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing Performance | Bazel\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/rules/performance\"},{\"title\":\"Android Build Performance | Bazel\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/docs/android-build-performance\"},{\"title\":\"Fun with Flags. The bazel build system, originally an… | by Doug Rabson | CodeX | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/codex/fun-with-flags-8c137052e245\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization flags are ignored in builds · Issue #21528 · tensorflow/tensorflow\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/21528\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/bazel/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/bazel/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Android Build Performance - Bazel main\",\"url\":\"https://docs.bazel.build/versions/main/android-build-performance.html\"},{\"title\":\"Optimize Iteration Speed | Bazel\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/advanced/performance/iteration-speed\"},{\"title\":\"Configurable Build Attributes | Bazel\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/docs/configurable-attributes\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for information about Google OR-Tools internal build flags, Bazel BUILD files, and optimization. Here are the results:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**OR-Tools Bazel Build Support:**\nOR-Tools comes with a Bazel-based build (WORKSPACE) that can be used on a wide range of platforms and is available for free from bazel.build. OR-Tools requires Bazel >= 5.4.0 and a compiler with C++17 support.\n\n**Bazel Compilation Modes:**\nThe --compilation_mode option (often shortened to -c, especially -c opt) takes an argument of fastbuild, dbg or opt, and affects various C/C++ code-generation options, such as the level of optimization and the completeness of debug tables. The \"opt\" mode means build with optimization enabled and with assert() calls disabled (-O2 -DNDEBUG).\n\n**Bazel Optimization Flags:**\nBazel provides the option to specify compiler and linker flags via --cxxopt, --copt, --conlyopt, --linkopt from the command line or .bazelrc file. In AOSP, cc toolchain features are used to specify features for rule targets, where each feature can enable multiple flag_sets unique to specific types of actions such as c compile, cpp compile, ar, and linking.\n\n**Build Performance Optimization:**\nWhen rolling up information from rule dependencies you should use depsets, only using plain lists or dicts to publish information local to the current rule, as a depset represents information as a nested graph which enables sharing.\n\nThe search results provide information about general Bazel optimization practices and OR-Tools' use of Bazel, but don't contain specific details about OR-Tools' internal build flags or private release optimization settings.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b3b11fbf-b013-421d-9d60-347aeefb2783","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:47.013Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"908c9e42-eb4d-49ca-9334-1bee16279f1a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
