{"parentUuid":"e3c7294d-9b6e-4e28-afcd-029b773475c7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014aoWfgPEKV78iR9t9ND6Yh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gwtvtx8fyDjenLw2Lmvxu1","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Rust FFI C++ bindings cxx workshop overhead callback constraint solver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3533,"cache_read_input_tokens":52170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3533,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotu4fqoWMzJkaMmktGT","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f7aa5f4-57b4-4675-9d46-55be6a2c8da1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:02.659Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8f7aa5f4-57b4-4675-9d46-55be6a2c8da1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gwtvtx8fyDjenLw2Lmvxu1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Rust FFI C++ bindings cxx workshop overhead callback constraint solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FFI - The Rustonomicon\",\"url\":\"https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/ffi.html\"},{\"title\":\"cxx - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cxx\"},{\"title\":\"CXX — safe interop between Rust and C++\",\"url\":\"https://cxx.rs/\"},{\"title\":\"Rust and Cpp interoperability | Kuczma.dev\",\"url\":\"https://kuczma.dev/articles/rust-and-cpp/\"},{\"title\":\"CXX — safe FFI between Rust and C++\",\"url\":\"https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/rust/cxx/+/232a0e3/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"C++/Rust FFI in 2025: Safe Interop with cxx Bridge | Markaicode\",\"url\":\"https://markaicode.com/cpp-rust-ffi-cxx-bridge-2025/\"},{\"title\":\"Generating Bindings to C++ - The bindgen User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-bindgen/cpp.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - rust-lang/rust-bindgen: Automatically generates Rust FFI bindings to C (and some C++) libraries. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-bindgen\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dtolnay/cxx: Safe interop between Rust and C++ · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dtolnay/cxx\"},{\"title\":\"Mix in Rust with C++ - Blog - Tweede golf\",\"url\":\"https://tweedegolf.nl/en/blog/135/mix-in-rust-with-c++\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Rust FFI with C++ bindings using CXX and related topics:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**CXX Library Overview:**\nCXX provides a safe mechanism for calling C++ code from Rust and Rust code from C++. The resulting FFI bridge operates at zero or negligible overhead, with no copying, no serialization, no memory allocation, and no runtime checks needed.\n\n**Workshop & Overhead Performance:**\nRecent performance results show that CXX Bridge adds minimal overhead for data-intensive operations, with vector operations showing only 1.05x overhead compared to direct C++, making it suitable for performance-critical code.\n\n**Callback Support:**\nThe search results indicate that CXX supports Rust callbacks for C++. While direct function pointers have limitations, workarounds exist such as defining a C++ class with a pure virtual method, implementing a strongly typed listener/observer pattern.\n\n**Constraint Solver & Static Analysis:**\nCXX uses static analysis of types and function signatures to protect both Rust's and C++'s invariants, then uses code generators to implement the boundary efficiently with static assertions for verifying correctness. The static analysis detects and prevents passing types by value that shouldn't be passed from C++ to Rust, particularly those containing internal pointers.\n\nThe search results show that CXX is a robust solution for safe Rust-C++ interoperability with minimal performance overhead and compile-time safety guarantees.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"10a93164-5fee-4883-aaac-70b63cd7d066","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:10.383Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f7aa5f4-57b4-4675-9d46-55be6a2c8da1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e3c7294d-9b6e-4e28-afcd-029b773475c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0f373ebb-a92e-4bba-8942-d03ed7b7aa78","agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012zPeQ8WH5mHJtzWY7BwFT9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"JIT compiled SAT propagator specialized constraint solver code generation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Propagation via Lazy Clause Generation*\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/COMP90046/resources/lazyj.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT Documentation Release 1.9.dev2\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/pysat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solvers’ API (pysat.solvers) — PySAT 1.9.dev2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Decomposing Global Grammar Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-74970-7_42\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Boolean Constraint Propagation for Efficient SAT-Solving on FPGAs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2401.07429v2\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about JIT-compiled SAT propagators and specialized constraint solver code generation:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Lazy Clause Generation and SAT Propagators\n\nPropagators can be converted to lazy clause generators for a SAT solver, which is a foundational approach in this area. CP-SAT uses a CDCL (Conflict-Driven Clause Learning) SAT solver that is extended to handle integer variables and complex constraints through a technique called \"lazy clause generation.\"\n\n### Specialized Constraint Solvers\n\nThe search results show that specialized constraints for common patterns propagate effectively, and CP-SAT includes specialized propagators for different constraint types. CP-SAT provides specialized constraint types that propagate far more effectively than decomposing problems into elementary constraints. The AllDifferent constraint ensures all variables in a set take different values. For n variables with domains of size d, the naive decomposition into pairwise inequalities requires n(n-1)/2 constraints and propagates weakly.\n\n### Constraint Propagator Architecture\n\nUsers can define their own propagation engines, i.e. constraint propagators, attachable to a SAT solver. The implementation of this functionality builds on the use of the IPASIR-UP interface, which enables extensible propagator support.\n\n### Hardware Acceleration Approaches\n\nFor performance optimization, hardware-accelerated SAT solvers targeting processor/Field Programmable Gate Arrays (FPGA) SoCs accelerate the most expensive subroutine of the Davis-Putnam-Logemann-Loveland (DPLL) algorithm, Boolean Constraint Propagation (BCP) through fine-grained FPGA parallelism.\n\nThe search results don't specifically address JIT compilation of propagators, but they show the broader ecosystem of specialized constraint solvers and propagator architectures used in modern SAT-based solving systems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"64d85a91-e9ef-43a6-b385-2f296684f635","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:11:10.768Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3c7294d-9b6e-4e28-afcd-029b773475c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"64d85a91-e9ef-43a6-b385-2f296684f635","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa2cd8e2e60b20719","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GveChwvfxDbq1degBD9PJ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have sufficient research. Let me synthesize the findings.\n\n---\n\n# 编译器优化路径调研报告（CP-SAT 加速）\n\n## 总览表：编译器优化 / 工具 / 加速预估 / 工程量 / 风险\n\n| 路径 | 加速预估（CP-SAT 类） | 工程量 | 风险 | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `-O3` (默认 Release `-O2`) | +0~3% | 极低（改一行） | 低，偶发 UB 暴露 | OR-Tools Release 已 `-O2/O3` 默认开 |\n| `-march=native -mtune=native` | +3~6% | 低（改 CMake flag） | 二进制不可移植；Round 4 已确认 13900KS 无 AVX-512，主要靠 AVX2/BMI2 | x86 主要受益 watched-literal 位运算、bitset、CRC |\n| `-flto=thin` (Clang) / `-flto` (GCC) | +3~10% | 中（链接耗时翻倍） | thin 比 full 安全，full 偶尔 ICE | LTO 让跨 TU 的 propagator inline 成立 |\n| MSVC `/GL` + `/LTCG` | +5~25%（JetBrains clangd 测得 25%） | 中 | MSVC 兼容性最好 | Windows 不需要换 toolchain |\n| PGO (instrumented，Clang `-fprofile-generate`/`-use`) | +5~15%（branch-heavy 实测 +13%） | **高**（双 build + corpus + 重 build） | corpus 不代表生产 → 反优化；Clang/MSVC 体验最好 | 我们是分支密集型，受益面最大 |\n| GCC PGO | +5~10% | 高 | GCC PGO 在 Windows MinGW 下脆弱 | Linux 优先 |\n| LLVM BOLT (post-link) | 在 LTO+PGO 上再 +5~8%（Meta 数据中心实测最高 +20%） | 中（仅 Linux x86） | Windows/MSVC 不支持 | 只在 Linux 上有意义 |\n| `-DNDEBUG` 关 assertion | +1~3% | 极低（Release 默认已开） | 无 | 已默认 |\n| auto-vectorization 单独效果 | +0~2% on CP-SAT | — | — | propagator 内循环是分支密集 + 间接寻址，watched literal 不能向量化；只有 LP simplex 内部 dense loop 受益 |\n| Cython 重写 outer search loop | 0%（不是瓶颈） | 高 | **基本无意义** | OR-Tools C++ 占 99% 时间，Python 只是 RPC |\n| Numba | 0% | — | 完全不进 OR-Tools 内部 | 排除 |\n| Rust FFI 重写 outer | 0% | 极高 | 同上 | 排除，除非要换 SAT 后端 |\n| JIT 专用 propagator | 学术原型，无 CP-SAT 接入 | 极高（自己写引擎） | 工程量数月 | 排除 |\n| Apple Silicon (M3 Max + clang LTO+PGO) | 与 Linux x86 相当或略低 | 同 Linux | ARM NEON 不替代 AVX2，但 IPC 更高 | 平台切换成本高 |\n\n**Round 2/4 的 +15~35% 加速来源拆解（自我估计）**：Linux 调度/glibc malloc +5~10%，编译器路径 +6~15%（march+LTO+PGO 累加），其余来自 NUMA/THP/CPU governor。**Windows 自编 OR-Tools 能拿到的部分约 +8~15%（march+LTO+PGO 不靠 OS）**。\n\n---\n\n## 自编 OR-Tools 9.15 + PGO 操作清单（Linux 优先，Windows 也走通）\n\n### Linux + Clang 18 路径（推荐）\n\n```bash\n# 0. 准备\ngit clone -b stable https://github.com/google/or-tools && cd or-tools\ngit checkout v9.15\n\n# 1. Stage 1: instrumented build\ncmake -S . -B build_pgo_gen -G Ninja \\\n  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_DEPS=ON \\\n  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang-18 -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++-18 \\\n  -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"-O3 -march=native -mtune=native -fprofile-generate=/tmp/ortools_prof -DNDEBUG\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=\"-fprofile-generate=/tmp/ortools_prof\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS=\"-fprofile-generate=/tmp/ortools_prof\"\ncmake --build build_pgo_gen -j\n\n# 2. 跑 corpus（关键：用我们项目的真实负载）\nmkdir -p /tmp/ortools_prof\n# corpus 建议（按代表性排序，总跑 30~60 min）：\n#   - 5 个 valley4 70x70 wave 检查点（小、中、大 Benders 迭代）\n#   - 1 个 mandatory_exact_instances 全跑\n#   - 1 个 routing_subproblem 紧张 case\n#   - 1 个 binding_subproblem 退化 case\n#   - 1 个 master_model 仅占位无路由 case\n# ⚠️ 不要混入 unsat 早退案例（分布偏差大，会反优化）\npython main.py --campaign-hours 1.0 --pgo-corpus  # 你需要加这个 flag 让 outer 自动跑代表样本\n\n# 3. 合并 .profraw\nllvm-profdata-18 merge -output=/tmp/ortools.profdata /tmp/ortools_prof/*.profraw\n\n# 4. Stage 2: optimized build\ncmake -S . -B build_pgo_use -G Ninja \\\n  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_DEPS=ON -DBUILD_PYTHON=ON \\\n  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang-18 -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++-18 \\\n  -DCMAKE_INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION=ON \\\n  -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"-O3 -march=native -mtune=native -flto=thin -fprofile-use=/tmp/ortools.profdata -Wno-backend-plugin -DNDEBUG\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=\"-flto=thin -fprofile-use=/tmp/ortools.profdata\"\ncmake --build build_pgo_use -j\n\n# 5. （可选）BOLT post-link\nperf record -e cycles:u -j any,u -o perf.data -- ./build_pgo_use/bin/sat_runner ...\nperf2bolt build_pgo_use/lib/libortools.so -p perf.data -o ortools.bolt.fdata\nllvm-bolt build_pgo_use/lib/libortools.so -o libortools.bolt.so -data=ortools.bolt.fdata \\\n  -reorder-blocks=ext-tsp -reorder-functions=hfsort+ -split-functions -split-all-cold -split-eh -dyno-stats\n\n# 6. 安装到 venv\ncmake --install build_pgo_use --prefix ~/.local/ortools_pgo\npip install build_pgo_use/python  # 或对应 wheel\n```\n\n### Windows + clang-cl / MSVC 路径\n\n- 用 `clang-cl` 比 MSVC 自带 PGO 体验好（参考 JetBrains 实测 clang-cl LTO+PGO = 35% 提速）。\n- Stage 1 flag：`-Xclang -fprofile-instr-generate`\n- MSVC 原生路径：`/GL /LTCG:PGINSTRUMENT` → 跑 corpus → `/LTCG:PGOPTIMIZE`\n- 注意：x64 Native Tools Command Prompt，路径不能含空格（OR-Tools 官方明确警告）。\n- BOLT 不可用（Windows 无 perf）。\n\n### Corpus 大小经验值\n\n- LLVM 自身 PGO corpus 大概 ~5 min check-clang + 一个完整 LLVM rebuild。\n- 我们 70×70 + 266 设施一个完整 wave 大概 30-90 min，**跑 5-10 个有代表性的 wave 就够**（总 corpus 大小 50-200 MB .profraw）。\n- 关键原则（LLVM 官方）：\"PGO does best when the profiles gathered represent how the user plans to use the compiler\" — 用真实 valley4 campaign 数据，不要用合成 toy。\n\n---\n\n## 关键链接\n\n- [OR-Tools CMake README (stable)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/cmake/README.md)\n- [OR-Tools C++ Build on Windows (官方)](https://developers.google.com/optimization/install/cpp/source_windows)\n- [LLVM PGO 官方教程](https://llvm.org/docs/HowToBuildWithPGO.html)\n- [JetBrains C++ LTO/PGO 实测对比 (clangd)](https://blog.jetbrains.com/clion/2022/05/testing-3-approaches-performance-cpp_apps/) — clang-cl LTO+PGO = +35%\n- [LLVM BOLT README](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/bolt/README.md)\n- [BOLT 论文 (Meta，arxiv)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.06735) — 编译器类工作负载 +20.4% on top of LTO+FDO\n- [PGO 综述论文 (arxiv 2507.16649)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16649) — 通用工作负载 5-30%，分支密集 +13%\n- [Intel Hardware-PGO](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/hwpgo.html) — LBR 采样 PGO 拿到 instrumentation 80-93% 收益但 <2% overhead\n- [CMake CheckIPOSupported](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/module/CheckIPOSupported.html) — 跨平台 LTO 正确写法\n- [CXX (Rust-C++ FFI)](https://cxx.rs/) — 1.05x overhead，但对我们项目无意义\n- [CP-SAT Primer \"Under the hood\"](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html) — 确认 CP-SAT 是 LCG 架构\n\n---\n\n## 对我们项目的优先级建议\n\n**第一档（值得做，ROI 高）：**\n1. **`-march=native + -flto=thin + LTO via CMake INTERPROCEDURAL_OPTIMIZATION`**：低工程量，预期 +6~12%，Linux/Windows 都能拿。先做这个验证整个自编流水线。\n2. **PGO（用真实 valley4 corpus）**：在 (1) 之上再叠 +5~10%。工程量 1~2 天。但必须 Linux + Clang 走通才稳定，Windows MSVC PGO 流水线脆弱。\n\n**第二档（看情况）：**\n3. **Linux 迁移 + BOLT**：BOLT 只在 Linux 有，post-link 再 +5~8%。和 Round 2 提的 Linux 迁移耦合。如果你已经在做 Linux 路径，把 BOLT 算进去；如果不迁，就跳过。\n4. **OR-Tools 9.15 → main 主线**：自编已经必须 git clone，顺手追主线能拿 propagator 上游修复，但和编译器优化无关。\n\n**第三档（明确不做，浪费时间）：**\n5. **Cython / Numba / Rust 重写 outer**：你的 outer search loop Python 占比 < 1%，瓶颈是 OR-Tools C++ 内部。重写 0 收益。\n6. **JIT 专用 propagator**：学术原型，没有可用工程接入。\n7. **AVX-512 / AVX-VNNI 改造**：13900KS 无 AVX-512，AVX-VNNI 是 INT8 神经网络指令，对 SAT propagator 无用。\n8. **追求 auto-vectorization on propagator**：watched literal lookup 是控制流密集 + 间接寻址，编译器 vectorize 不到 hot path。`-march=native` 已经把能拿的 SIMD 拿到了。\n\n**总收益预估**：在 Windows 不动 OS 的前提下，自编 OR-Tools + march=native + LTO + PGO 大约 **+10~20%**。叠加 Linux 迁移 + BOLT 大约 **+15~30%**。这跟 Round 2 的 +15~35% 估计吻合，且能把\"Linux 红利\"和\"编译器红利\"分清楚——编译器路径占 2/3，OS 路径占 1/3。\n\n工程预算建议：先花 1 天把 `march=native + LTO` 的 CMake 走通跑 benchmark，能看到 +5% 就继续上 PGO，看不到就直接停手，因为 PGO 的 ROI 系数比 LTO 小但工程量大 5x。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1664,"cache_read_input_tokens":55703,"output_tokens":4689,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1664},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1161,"output_tokens":4689,"cache_read_input_tokens":55703,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1664,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caotv1i2QnF3RVWMXJLFu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2bb73892-3b7c-4f11-a17a-61a1dc680f51","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:12:28.497Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
